{
  "name": "Playtest God Mode",
  "description": "Full Randomizer plus an unkillable party, for clearing the game quickly to verify the randomizers that only show up later: shop stock, drop tables and the rest. Every playable character gets ATK/POW +250, GRT/DEF +200, HP +500, Speed +100 and PP +50 at every level, so nothing misses and nothing survives. This is a test build, not a way to play. NOTE 2026-10-12: the per-character 'fatigue' entries were removed. They had never done anything: stat_curve's `bonus` used to add a flat amount to every row of the Adv_ table, which leaves every gap between levels unchanged and so leaves the character's actual stats exactly as they were. When `bonus` was fixed to write the starting line in creatures.GDA instead, fatigue had no creature column to write - PP's base is columns 11/12 and belongs to pp_curve - so the profile stopped building. Removing them restores the build and changes no behavior, because there was none. To actually raise PP here, add a pp_curve block with `base` and/or `per_level`; it is left out rather than guessed at a value.",
